/*

* ============================================================================
* 42. DOMAIN-NEUTRAL SEMANTIC BOUNDARY
* ============================================================================
* 
* The following invariant is mandatory:
* 
* grammar
*     |
*     v
* parser context
*     |
*     v
* domain-neutral AST
*     |
*     v
* semantic tensor/data model
*     |
*     v
* canonical IR
* 
* The grammar must never directly construct:
* 
* TensorIR
* DataTensorIR
* GPUIR
* CUDAIR
* QPUDataIR
* VendorTensorIR
* 
* ============================================================================
* 43. FUTURE EXTENSION CONTRACT
* ============================================================================
* 
* Future tensor data features must prefer:
* 
* existing expression syntax
* existing type syntax
* existing name syntax
* existing attribute syntax
* existing resource syntax
* existing capability syntax
* existing tensor grammar
* 
* before introducing a new parser rule.
* 
* A new rule is justified only when a construct has genuinely distinct
* language-level syntax or semantic boundaries.
* 
* New tensor algorithms MUST NOT require new grammar rules merely because
* their names are new.
* 
* ============================================================================
* 44. ERROR / DIAGNOSTIC CONTRACT
* ============================================================================
* 
* This grammar is responsible only for structural parse errors.
* 
* Semantic diagnostics belong downstream and should distinguish:
* 
* invalid tensor type
* incompatible element type
* incompatible shape
* invalid rank relationship
* invalid dimension
* invalid operation
* unsupported capability
* unavailable resource
* invalid serialization
* invalid materialization
* invalid distribution
* invalid partitioning
* invalid replication
* 
* Diagnostics must preserve source locations from the parser/frontend.
* 
* ============================================================================
* 45. COMPATIBILITY CONTRACT
* ============================================================================
* 
* Compatibility must distinguish:
* 
* source compatibility
* semantic compatibility
* AST compatibility
* IR compatibility
* serialization compatibility
* backend compatibility
* 
* A backend change must not require a grammar change unless the source
* language itself changes.
* 
* ============================================================================
* 46. TEST CONTRACT
* ============================================================================
* 
* The owning test suite MUST cover:
* 
* POSITIVE:
* 
* - tensor-valued expressions;
* - tensor literals;
* - tensor construction;
* - tensor operations;
* - symbolic shapes;
* - nested tensor values;
* - tensor metadata;
* - tensor transformations;
* - tensor materialization intent;
* - tensor serialization intent;
* - resource/capability expressions;
* - tensor values inside records;
* - tensor values inside collections;
* - tensor values inside streams;
* - tensor values in AI programs;
* - tensor values in classical programs;
* - tensor values surrounding quantum computation.
* 
* NEGATIVE:
* 
* - malformed tensor boundaries;
* - malformed argument lists;
* - malformed metadata;
* - malformed shape syntax;
* - malformed bindings;
* - malformed materialization syntax;
* - malformed serialization syntax.
* 
* BOUNDARY:
* 
* - scalar tensor;
* - one-dimensional tensor;
* - nested tensors;
* - symbolic dimensions;
* - very large generated dimension lists;
* - deeply nested valid syntax;
* - long operation argument lists.
* 
* SCALABILITY:
* 
* - increasing tensor rank;
* - increasing dimension count;
* - increasing tensor declarations;
* - increasing operation count;
* - increasing metadata count;
* - increasing pipeline composition.
* 
* PORTABILITY:
* 
* The same source must parse independently of:
* 
* CPU
* GPU
* FPGA
* accelerator
* QPU
* node count
* memory capacity
* storage system
* provider
* topology.
* 
* DETERMINISM:
* 
* Identical source and grammar/version configuration must produce equivalent
* parse structures independent of execution hardware.
* 
* ============================================================================
* 47. HARD-CODING AUDIT
* ============================================================================
* 
* Release validation MUST reject accidental introduction of:
* 
* MAX_TENSOR_RANK
* MAX_TENSOR_DIMENSIONS
* MAX_TENSOR_ELEMENTS
* MAX_TENSOR_SIZE
* MAX_MEMORY
* MAX_DEVICES
* MAX_NODES
* MAX_PARTITIONS
* MAX_REPLICAS
* MAX_THREADS
* MAX_GPUS
* MAX_FPGAS
* MAX_QUBITS
* 
* and equivalent fixed-capacity grammar constructs.
* 
* Numeric literals in source remain program semantics.
* 
